  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Country programme for inclusive and sustainable industrial development 2023 # 2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNIDO#s activities in India are guided by a Country Programme (CP), an overarching framework that provides a vision for advancing the UNIDO-India partnership, highlighting key industrial development priorities, direction for new partnerships and projects and support to national schemes and initiatives.  UNIDO#s interventions under CP 2023-2027 aim to support the Government of India (Gol) in its efforts to make India a global manufacturing hub, in ways that maximize economic growth, employment and environmental safeguarding, thereby contributing to progress towards achieving the vision of #Viksit Bharat @ 2047# (Developed India). The CP is also aligned with, and derived from, the agreed priorities of the United Nations in India, as established under the India United Nations Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UNSDCF) 2023-2027. As a framework grounded in established national priorities and cognizant of emerging megatrends relevant to industrialization, the CP is expected to guide the further programming, implementation, monitoring and evaluation of UNIDO&apos;s interventions in India during 2023-2027.</narrative>
  </description>
